mber":574,"title":"[FEATURE]","comments":7,"created_at":"2025-09-06T15:45:14Z"},{"number":25,"title":"Auto generating Table","comments":7,"created_at":"2024-04-10T04:01:12Z"},{"number":17,"title":"Can ER diagram of already created database be created automagically?","comments":7,"created_at":"2024-04-07T18:06:38Z"},{"number":655,"title":"[BUG] Impossible to share (self hosted DrawDB)","comments":6,"created_at":"2025-10-18T19:48:15Z"},{"number":298,"title":"[BUG]表连接发生错乱","comments":6,"created_at":"2024-11-13T04:49:12Z"}],"discussions":[{"number":1088,"title":"Is there a way to export the schema diagram as an image file directly, or is SQL the only export option currently?","comments":2,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-08-03T20:37:43Z"},{"number":1087,"title":"Is there a name for the JSON export format?","comments":1,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-08-03T15:31:52Z"},{"number":1083,"title":"Two different JSON shapes for the same diagram. Why?","comments":2,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-07-27T19:39:02Z"},{"number":1064,"title":"Automatically generate references to foreign keys","comments":1,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-07-02T03:07:17Z"},{"number":834,"title":"Movement?","comments":1,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-01-07T17:48:15Z"},{"number":664,"title":"MCP ?","comments":1,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2025-10-28T12:01:05Z"},{"number":614,"title":"HOW DO I TURN OFF NOTIFICATIONS","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2025-10-04T21:37:04Z"},{"number":507,"title":"Typescript","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2025-06-23T11:40:15Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"v1.9.0 - Import from your database","tag":"v1.9.0","published_at":"2026-11-01T17:54:52Z","body":"## Import from your database\r\n\r\n**File → Import from database.** Pick your dialect, copy the read-only query drawDB gives you, run it in the SQL client you already use (psql, Workbench, DBeaver, SSMS…), and paste the result back. drawDB draws the diagram and auto-arranges it.\r\n\r\n- Works with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, SQL Server, SQLite and Oracle\r\n- No connection string: your credentials never leave your machine, and drawDB never sees row data\r\n\r\n(#1182)\r\n\r\n## Subject areas that hold tables\r\n\r\nAreas now own the tables inside them: move an area and its tables move with it, hide or show a whole group at once, and reorder areas. (#1184, #1185)\r\n\r\n## Also in this release\r\n\r\n- Faster canvas on large diagrams (#1172, #1183)\r\n- SQL headers tab: custom text at the top of every export (#1169)\r\n- Comments shown in the sidebar (#1159)\r\n- Touchpad horizontal panning without holding Shift (#1162)\r\n- Fix: import when `NOT NULL` is absent (#1171)\r\n- Fix: autosave for enum-only diagrams and empty edits (#1186)\r\n- Dependency updates\r\n\r\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/drawdb-io/drawdb/compare/v1.8.2...v1.9.0\r\n","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[],"stale":false,"snapshot_at":"2026-11-14T08:50:43Z","history_start":"2026-09-06"}